--  A TCP connection, as a stream in both directions (ADR 0007, section
--  3), so a command that takes a stream can be given one. Release closes
--  it in both directions (ADR 0010); releasing it again does nothing.
--
--  A Read waits until data arrives. net holds the request meanwhile, so
--  the wait stops only the caller. A Read that returns nothing is the end
--  of the stream (ADR 0011): the far end has closed its side.
--
--  After a restore the connection is closed, as if the far end had reset
--  it (section 6): every call but Release fails, and so does a Read that
--  was waiting.

interface Network.Connection : Streams.Stream, Common.Resource is

end Network.Connection;
